# @alymichwoo Content Studio

A personal content planning + analytics web app for a creator at the intersection
of CrossFit, lifestyle, AI, and human performance. Single user, maintained solo.

## Stack (do not deviate without asking)
- Frontend: React 18 + Vite + Tailwind CSS v3
- Data + auth: Supabase (Postgres, Auth, Row Level Security), called DIRECTLY from
  the React client. There is NO Node/Express backend.
- The only server-side code is one Supabase Edge Function added in Phase 4 to proxy
  the Anthropic API (so the API key is never in the browser).
- Hosting: Vercel (frontend) + Supabase.

## Required libraries (use these, don't substitute)
- Routing: react-router-dom
- Server data: @tanstack/react-query (never raw useEffect for fetching)
- Drag and drop: @dnd-kit/core (NOT react-beautiful-dnd)
- Forms + validation: react-hook-form + zod (+ @hookform/resolvers)
- Charts (Phase 3): recharts
- Dates: date-fns
- Icons: lucide-react
- PDF export (Phase 3): client-side via html2canvas + jspdf

## Code conventions
- Functional components + hooks. Clean, commented, modular — maintained solo.
- All Supabase calls live in hooks under src/hooks (usePosts, useEvents, etc.),
  never inline in components.
- Security lives in Postgres RLS, not client code. Every table is scoped by user_id
  with policy `auth.uid() = user_id`.
- Domain vocabulary (pillars, platforms, statuses, post types, colors) is defined
  ONCE in src/lib/constants.js and imported everywhere. Its string values must match
  the Postgres enums exactly.

## Brand & design (Unfiltered Athlete — raw, real, high performance)
- Palette: charcoal #1C1C1E (primary), coral #FF5733 (accent, used sparingly),
  cream #FAF9F6 (background), slate #8E8E93 (muted text/borders).
- Pillar colors: Train #378ADD, Live #D4537E, Think #7F77DD, Feel #1D9E75, Fuel #EF9F27.
- Font: DM Sans throughout. Headers heavy/uppercase with tight tracking for an
  athletic, editorial feel. Coral is a sharp accent, not a flood.
- Vibe: modern, minimal, confident. Not cutesy, not corporate.

## Data model (canonical — migrations must match this)
Enums:
- pillar: train | live | think | feel | fuel
- platform: tiktok | instagram | linkedin
- post_status: idea | drafting | ready | scheduled | posted
- post_type: reel | carousel | story | static | video
- schedule_type: event | travel | competition | launch | personal
- brand_status: prospect | active | past
- campaign_status: pitching | negotiating | active | delivered | wrapped
- payment_status: unpaid | paid

Tables (every table has user_id + RLS `auth.uid() = user_id`, except profiles which
is keyed by id):
- profiles(id=auth.users.id, display_name, handle, created_at)
- posts(id, user_id, title, caption, hook, notes, platforms platform[], pillar,
    post_type, series, status, scheduled_date, posted_date,
    deliverable_id -> deliverables (nullable, on delete set null),
    archived bool, created_at, updated_at)
- schedule_items(id, user_id, title, type schedule_type, start_date, end_date,
    location, notes, created_at)  -- multi-day, calendar context only
- brands(id, user_id, name, website, contact_name, contact_email, logo_url, notes,
    status brand_status, created_at)
- campaigns(id, user_id, brand_id, title, status campaign_status, start_date,
    end_date, brief, compensation, payment_status, disclosure_required bool,
    created_at, updated_at)
- deliverables(id, user_id, campaign_id, platform, post_type, quantity_required,
    due_date, notes)
- metrics(id, user_id, post_id, platform, recorded_at, views, likes, comments,
    shares, saves, impressions, reach, reactions, reposts, follows_gained,
    profile_visits, created_at)  -- explicit sparse per-platform columns

## Key product decisions (don't re-litigate)
- Posts can target multiple platforms. Metrics are tracked per platform, so one post
  can have several metric rows.
- Captions: plain textarea with a live per-platform character counter. No rich text.
- Engagement rate is COMPUTED IN CODE (never stored), per platform:
    tiktok    = (likes + comments + shares) / views
    instagram = (likes + comments + saves) / reach
    linkedin  = (reactions + comments + reposts) / impressions
- Posts link to a specific deliverable (deliverable-level linking) so a brief shows
  progress like "2 of 3 reels delivered".
- Schedule items (events/travel/competitions) are visual calendar context in v1 and
  become inputs to the Phase 4 AI assistant later.
- The AI assistant (Phase 4) lives behind a Supabase Edge Function. Keep a src/ai/
  folder as the integration seam; build the real thing in Phase 4 only.

## Working style
- Build only what the current step asks for. If something is complex, propose a
  simpler v1 first. Ask before adding libraries or changing the stack/schema.